So we have two dogs and this year they were ketchup and mustard.

1146
01:06:03.070 --> 01:06:04.230
Oh, I love it.

1147
01:06:04.370 --> 01:06:06.290
Oh, I would love to see a picture of that.

1148
01:06:06.350 --> 01:06:07.970
That lights up Angela's life.

1149
01:06:08.270 --> 01:06:09.510
It really does.

1150
01:06:09.530 --> 01:06:11.090
So wait, animals dressed like other animals.

1151
01:06:11.110 --> 01:06:14.390
You mean like, like a, like a dog dressed like a cow or like.

1152
01:06:14.610 --> 01:06:14.910
Oh yeah.

1153
01:06:15.010 --> 01:06:17.990
Or like a teddy bear that's, but it has like a bunny hat.

1154
01:06:19.210 --> 01:06:19.570
Yeah.

1155
01:06:19.710 --> 01:06:19.970
Fantastic.

1156
01:06:20.090 --> 01:06:20.370
I know.

1157
01:06:20.570 --> 01:06:20.730
Why?

1158
01:06:25.410 --> 01:06:29.050
Mike, thank you so much for coming on Office Ladies today.

1159
01:06:29.190 --> 01:06:30.110
This was such a treat.

1160
01:06:30.370 --> 01:06:33.570
We want to tell people that you wrote a book.

1161
01:06:34.090 --> 01:06:34.530
Yes.

1162
01:06:34.690 --> 01:06:36.670
And the book is called How to Be Perfect.

1163
01:06:36.810 --> 01:06:39.590
It comes out on January 25th.

1164
01:06:40.030 --> 01:06:41.170
Tell us about it.

1165
01:06:41.670 --> 01:06:48.110
So this book came out of the show, The Good Place that I created, which was about, it's

1166
01:06:48.110 --> 01:06:51.990
a, if you haven't seen it, it's very hard to explain it in one sentence, but it's essentially

1167
01:06:51.990 --> 01:06:55.590
a, I pitched it as a show about like what it means to be a good person.

1168
01:06:55.870 --> 01:07:04.370
And for the show, I read a lot of ethics and philosophy by a lot of very old, boring people.

1169
01:07:04.370 --> 01:07:09.910
And I thought, I had this thought while I was researching it, which was that these people

1170
01:07:09.910 --> 01:07:12.610
have such good ideas for how to be better people.

1171
01:07:12.810 --> 01:07:17.150
Like as all of these ethical theories and this moral philosophy is like, it's like a how

1172
01:07:17.150 --> 01:07:22.350
to guide for like living a good life and being a good person on earth, but their writing

1173
01:07:22.350 --> 01:07:25.210
is so tortured and boring that it, that no one wants to read it.

1174
01:07:25.350 --> 01:07:30.510
So maybe I could write a version where I sort of try to explain as best as I can what their

1175
01:07:30.510 --> 01:07:34.010
theories are, but in a way that doesn't give you a tension headache.

1176
01:07:34.370 --> 01:07:35.430
And make you sleepy.

1177
01:07:35.690 --> 01:07:36.930
So that's what it is.

1178
01:07:37.010 --> 01:07:40.830
It's, it's sort of a summary of, of a lot of different theories and moral philosophy.

1179
01:07:41.010 --> 01:07:46.330
The way that the book is sort of organized is like, I pose a bunch of boring questions

1180
01:07:46.330 --> 01:07:49.730
or mundane questions that, that face us every day.

1181
01:07:49.850 --> 01:07:53.810
Like if my friend bought an ugly shirt and says, what do you think of my shirt?

1182
01:07:53.910 --> 01:07:59.370
Is it okay to lie to her or, or can you, or can you, um, or do you have to tell the truth?

1183
01:07:59.590 --> 01:08:03.010
And so it's questions like that, that are just things that come up in everyday life.

1184
01:08:03.010 --> 01:08:07.830
And then I try to explain what like different moral philosophers and ethicists would say

1185
01:08:07.830 --> 01:08:08.650
about those questions.

1186
01:08:09.150 --> 01:08:12.010
Um, so that's the idea and it's on sale January.

1187
01:08:12.230 --> 01:08:12.890
It's on sale now.

1188
01:08:13.090 --> 01:08:16.090
You can buy it now from any online bookstore that you prefer.

1189
01:08:16.090 --> 01:08:20.890
Um, and also all of the, uh, uh, proceeds are going to charity.

1190
01:08:20.890 --> 01:08:26.090
So you can buy it and know that you're, uh, doing something good in the world by having

1191
01:08:26.090 --> 01:08:26.810
money go to charity.

1192
01:08:26.930 --> 01:08:28.050
Oh, I love that.

1193
01:08:28.330 --> 01:08:31.590
Just by buying the book, I am being a good person.

1194
01:08:31.670 --> 01:08:32.010
That's right.

1195
01:08:32.310 --> 01:08:32.410
That's right.

1196
01:08:32.510 --> 01:08:33.150
That's the idea.

1197
01:08:33.330 --> 01:08:33.430
Yeah.

1198
01:08:33.430 --> 01:08:36.750
So you're really setting me up to succeed.

1199
01:08:36.910 --> 01:08:36.970
I know.

1200
01:08:37.290 --> 01:08:38.250
I like it.

1201
01:08:38.310 --> 01:08:38.870
I like it too.

1202
01:08:39.390 --> 01:08:43.550
You know, right away that you've made the world a slightly better place just by buying

1203
01:08:43.550 --> 01:08:43.950
the book.

1204
01:08:44.310 --> 01:08:45.370
It's that easy.

1205
01:08:45.530 --> 01:08:46.810
It's that easy to be a good person.

1206
01:08:46.990 --> 01:08:47.830
I love it.

1207
01:08:47.970 --> 01:08:50.490
Well, this is what Mindy Kaling had to say about your book.

1208
01:08:50.610 --> 01:08:56.770
She said, as someone who worries that a deep dive into morality will ruin my fun and problematic

1209
01:08:56.770 --> 01:08:57.290
life.

1210
01:08:57.290 --> 01:08:59.670
I was certain this book wouldn't be for me.

1211
01:08:59.890 --> 01:09:01.290
Boy, was I wrong.

1212
01:09:01.470 --> 01:09:04.050
It's so brilliant and funny and warmly written.

1213
01:09:04.050 --> 01:09:07.810
You don't realize you're becoming a better person just by reading it.

1214
01:09:08.810 --> 01:09:09.330
Yes.

1215
01:09:09.430 --> 01:09:11.630
It was very nice of her to blurb the book.

1216
01:09:11.790 --> 01:09:15.330
She's her blurb is actually the one that made the cover, which I don't think I've told it

1217
01:09:15.330 --> 01:09:16.950
Oh, cover blurb.

1218
01:09:17.010 --> 01:09:17.970
I found it online.

1219
01:09:18.270 --> 01:09:19.710
That's fancy blurb right there.

1220
01:09:20.590 --> 01:09:22.810
Well, I'm so excited to read it.

1221
01:09:23.050 --> 01:09:23.570
Yes.

1222
01:09:23.730 --> 01:09:26.830
I have ordered my copy and Angela has too.

1223
01:09:26.830 --> 01:09:27.990
And we're going to get them.

1224
01:09:28.290 --> 01:09:35.130
And Mike, thank you because I, well, I'm a huge fan of your Twitter as well.

1225
01:09:35.370 --> 01:09:35.590
Yeah.

1226
